⍝ Quad_NL.tc
⍝ ----------------------------------

⍝@ test3.

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs12.md #9, 2026-08-06): QuadFunction.cc
      ⍝ used to test a per-symbol NameClass (e.g. NC_VARIABLE == 2050,
      ⍝ NC_FUNCTION == 4099, NC_OPERATOR == 8196 -- NamedObject.hh) against
      ⍝ the requested-classes bitmap via "1 << nc" directly; shifting an int
      ⍝ by >= 32 is UB and only produced the right answer on x86 because the
      ⍝ hardware masks the shift count to 5 bits and every NameClass happens
      ⍝ to be a multiple of 32. The V1/V2/V3 (⎕NL 2), FOO (⎕NL 3) and OP1
      ⍝ (⎕NL 4) checks below already exercise exactly those NameClass values
      ⍝ end-to-end, so they double as the regression test for this fix
      ⍝ (masking the shift amount with NC_case_mask); UBSan is clean on all
      ⍝ of them after the fix.
      ⍝
      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      V1←1
      V2←2
      V3←3

      )ERASE OP1
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ GNU APL-only function header
∇ (LO OP1 RO) B
∇

      )ERASE FOO
      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
∇FOO
L1:
L2:
L3:
 '⎕NL 1:'   ◊ ⎕NL 1
 '⎕NL 2:'   ◊ ⎕NL 2
 '⎕NL 3:'   ◊ ⎕NL 3
 '⎕NL 4:'   ◊ ⎕NL 4
 '⎕NL 1 3:' ◊ ⎕NL 1 3
∇

      ⍝ monadic ----------------------------------

      FOO
⎕NL 1:
L1
L2
L3
⎕NL 2:
V1
V2
V3
⎕NL 3:
FOO
⎕NL 4:
OP1
⎕NL 1 3:
FOO
L1 
L2 
L3 

      ⍝ dyadic ----------------------------------

      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ ⎕LC/⎕NL depend on the test harness
      ⎕NL 2 3
FOO
V1 
V2 
V3 

      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      'V' ⎕NL 2 3
V1
V2
V3

      ⍝ ==================================


